<title>ITALY: Italy machine tool orders fall in Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Italy machine tool orders fall in Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian machine tool orders fell 5.2 percent in the first quarter of 1997, mainly due to a 21.1 percent slump in domestic demand, the machine tool producers' association UCIMU said.</p>
<p>&quot;A recovery in foreign orders, up 14.9 percent, was not enough to reverse the negative trend seen over the last six quarters,&quot; UCIMU said in a statement.</p>
<p>The last quarterly rise in orders was in the third quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
